# text = non sic Leucippis succendit Castora Phoebe, Pollucem cultu non Hilaira soror; non, Idae et cupido quondam discordia Phoebo, Eueni patriis filia litoribus; nec Phrygium falso traxit candore maritum avecta externis Hippodamia rotis : sed facies aderat nullis obnoxia gemmis, qualis Apelleis est color in tabulis.
# prose_translation = Not so did Phoebe, daughter of Leucippus, inflame Castor, nor did her sister Hilaira inflame Pollux with her beauty; not so did the daughter of Evenus, on her father's shores, once cause discord for Idas and for lustful Phoebus; nor did Hippodamia, carried off on foreign wheels, attract her Phrygian husband with false beauty; but a face was present that owed nothing to jewels, such as is the color in Apelles' paintings.
