# sent_id = 1.3.2
# text = hanc ego, nondum etiam sensus deperditus omnes, molliter impresso conor adire toro; et quamvis duplici correptum ardore iuberent hac Amor hac Liber, durus uterque deus, subiecto leviter positam temptare lacerto osculaque admota sumere et arma manu, non tamen ausus eram dominae turbare quietem, expertae metuens iurgia saevitiae ; sed sic intentis haerebam fixus ocellis, Argus ut ignotis cornibus Inachidos.
# prose_translation = This woman I, not yet having lost all my senses, try to approach on the softly pressed couch; and although Love here and Bacchus there, each a harsh god, would bid me, seized by a double passion, to test her lying lightly with my arm placed beneath and to take kisses and arms with my hand, yet I had not dared to disturb my mistress's rest, fearing the quarrels of her proven cruelty; but thus I clung fixed with intent eyes, like Argus at the unknown horns of Io.
# literal_translation = This woman I, not yet even senses having-lost all, softly having-been-pressed I-try to-approach couch; and although by-double seized passion they-would-order here Love here Bacchus, harsh each god, having-been-placed-under lightly lying to-test arm and-kisses having-been-brought-near to-take and arms with-hand, not however having-dared I-was to-disturb mistress's rest, having-been-experienced fearing quarrels cruelty; but thus with-intent I-clung fixed eyes, Argus as at-unknown horns of-Inachis.
