# sent_id = 1.7.1
# text = DVM tibi Cadmeae dicuntur, Pontice, Thebae armaque fraternae tristia militiae, atque, ita sim felix, primo contendis Homero, (sint modo fata tuis mollia carminibus :) nos, ut consuemus, nostros agitamus amores, atque aliquid duram quaerimus in dominam; nec tantum ingenio quantum servire dolori cogor et aetatis tempora dura queri.
# prose_translation = While Cadmean Thebes is being told by you, Ponticus, and the sad arms of fraternal warfare, and, so may I be fortunate, you compete with Homer first (only let the fates be gentle to your songs), we, as we are accustomed, pursue our loves, and seek something against a hard mistress; and I am compelled not so much by talent as to serve grief and to lament the harsh times of life.
# literal_translation = While to-you Cadmean Thebes are-told, Ponticus, and-arms of-brotherly sad warfare, and, so may-I-be fortunate, with-first Homer you-compete, (let-be only fates to-your gentle songs :) we, as we-are-accustomed, our loves we-drive, and something hard against-mistress we-seek; and not so-much by-talent as to-serve grief I-am-compelled and of-life times harsh to-lament.
