# sent_id = 1.7.4
# text = te quoque si certo puer hic concusserit arcu, (quod nolim nostros eviolasse deos) longe castra tibi, longe miser agmina septem flebis in aeterno surda iacere situ; et frustra cupies mollem componere versum, nec tibi subiciet carmina serus Amor.
# prose_translation = If this boy (Cupid) strikes you too with his sure bow—which I would not wish, that I have violated our gods—you will weep far off, wretched, that your camps and your seven battle-lines lie buried in eternal silence; and in vain you will desire to compose a soft verse, and late Love will not supply you songs.
# literal_translation = you also if with-certain this boy has-struck bow, (which I-would-not-wish our gods to-have-violated) far camps to-you, far wretched battle-lines seven you-will-weep in eternal deaf to-lie ruin; and in-vain you-will-desire soft to-compose verse, nor to-you will-subject songs late Love.
