# sent_id = 1.8a.8
# text = nam me non ullae poterunt corrumpere, de te quin ego, vita, tuo limine verba querar; nec me deficiet nautas rogitare citatos "Dicite, quo portu clausa puella mea est ?” et dicam "Licet atraciis et similia considat in oris, et licet Hylaeis, illa futura mea est."
# prose_translation = For no women will be able to corrupt me, so that I would not, my life, complain with words at your threshold about you; nor will it fail me to ask the swift sailors: "Tell me, in what harbor is my girl shut up?" And I will say: "Although she may settle on the shores of Attica and similar places, and although on the Hylaean shores, she will be mine."
# literal_translation = For me not any will-be-able to-corrupt, about you that I, life, at-your threshold words may-complain; nor will-fail me to-ask sailors swift "Tell, in what harbor shut-up girl my is?" and I-will-say "Although on-Attic and similar she-may-settle on shores, and although on-Hylaean, she future mine is."
