# prose_translation = And would that the little Lucrine boat, trusting in its tiny oars, might linger on the water, or that the wave, easy to yield to the alternating hand, might hold you enclosed in the slender wave of Teuthras, rather than that you, softly composed on the silent shore, should have leisure to hear the charming whispers of another, as a faithless girl is wont to slip away when her guard is removed, and not to remember the common gods: not because you are not known to me by reputation, but because in this matter all love is feared.
