# sent_id = 1.14.2
# text = nam sive optatam mecum trahit illa quietem, seu facili totum ducit amore diem, tum mihi Pactoli veniunt sub tecta liquores, et legitur Rubris gemma sub aequoribus; tum mihi cessuros spondent mea gaudia reges: quae maneant, dum me fata perire volent!
# prose_translation = For whether she draws the longed-for rest with me, or she spends the whole day in easy love, then the waters of Pactolus come under my roof, and a gem is picked from the Red Sea's depths; then my joys promise that kings will yield to me: may they remain, as long as the fates wish me to perish!
# literal_translation = For whether longed-for with-me she draws that rest, or with-easy whole she-spends love day, then to-me of-Pactolus come under roofs waters, and is-picked from-Red gem under seas; then to-me about-to-yield promise my joys kings: which may-they-remain, while me fates to-perish wish!
