# prose_translation = But you come slowly in my fear; and you can arrange yesterday's hair with your hands and seek a face with long idleness, and no less vary your breast with eastern gems, like a beautiful woman who prepares to go to a new husband: but not so was Calypso moved by the departure of Ulysses, she had wept once on the deserted seas: for many days she sat sad with uncombed hair, having spoken many things to the unjust sea, and although she would never see him after this, she grieved nevertheless, conscious of long joy.
