# text = quod mihi si tantum, Maecenas, fata dedissent, ut possem heroas ducere in arma manus, non ego Titanas canerem, non Ossan Olympo impositam, ut caeli Pelion esset iter, nec veteres Thebas, nec Pergama nomen Homeri, Xerxis et imperio bina coisse vada, regnave prima Remi aut animos Carthaginis altae, Cimbrorumque minas et benefacta Mari : bellaque resque tui memorarem Caesaris, et tu Caesare sub magno cura secunda fores.
# prose_translation = But if only the Fates had granted me so much, Maecenas, that I could lead heroic bands into arms, I would not sing of the Titans, nor of Ossa piled on Olympus, so that Pelion might be a path to heaven, nor ancient Thebes, nor Pergama, the theme of Homer, nor that the twin straits came together at Xerxes' command, nor the first kingdoms of Remus or the spirits of lofty Carthage, nor the threats of the Cimbri and the good deeds of Marius: I would recall the wars and deeds of your Caesar, and you would be his second concern under great Caesar.
