# prose_translation = For whenever I would sing of Mutina or Philippi, the tombs of citizens, or the naval battles of the Sicilian flight, and the overturned hearths of the ancient Etruscan race, and the captured shores of Ptolemaic Pharos, or would sing of Egypt and the Nile, when, dragged into the city, he went feeble with seven captive streams, or the necks of kings encircled with gilded chains, and the Actian beaks racing along the Sacred Way; my Muse would always weave you into those wars, and with peace taken up and laid down, a faithful head.
# literal_translation = For whenever Mutina or civil tombs Philippi or I-would-sing Sicilian naval wars of-flight, and-overturned hearths of-ancient race Etruscan, and of-Ptolemaic shores captured of-Pharos, or I-would-sing Egypt and Nile, when dragged into city with-seven captive waters he-went feeble, or of-kings with-gilded encircled necks chains, and-Actian in Sacred to-race beaks Way; you my Muse with-those always would-weave arms, and with-taken and with-laid-down peace faithful head :
