# prose_translation = Machaon healed the slow limbs of Philoctetes, and Chiron, son of Philyra, healed the eyes of Phoenix, and the Epidaurian god restored the dead Androgeon with Cretan herbs on his ancestral hearths, and the Mysian youth, with the very spear with which he had felt the wound, felt the cure.
