# sent_id = 2.8a.9
# text = viderat ille fugas, tractos in litore Achivos, fervere et Hectorea Dorica castra face; viderat informem multa Patroclon harena porrectum et sparsas caede iacere comas, omnia formosam propter Briseida passus : tantus in erepto saevit amore dolor.
# prose_translation = He had seen the routs, the Achaeans dragged along the shore, and the Doric camp seething with Hector's torch; he had seen Patroclus lying shapeless in much sand and his hair scattered with gore, having suffered all for beautiful Briseis: so great a grief rages over love that has been snatched away.
# literal_translation = He-had-seen that-one the-routs, dragged on the-shore Achaeans, to-boil and with-Hector's Doric camp torch; he-had-seen shapeless with-much Patroclus sand stretched-out and scattered with-slaughter to-lie hair, all for-beautiful Briseis having-suffered : so-great over-snatched-away love rages grief.
