# sent_id = 2.9.3
# text = nec non exanimem amplectens Briseis Achillen candida vesana verberat ora manu; et dominum lavit maerens captiva cruentum, propositum fluviis in Simoenta vadis, foedavitque comas, et tanti corpus Achilli maximaque in parva sustulit ossa manu; cum tibi nec Peleus aderat nec caerula mater, Scyria nec viduo Deidamia viro.
# prose_translation = Nor did Briseis, embracing the lifeless Achilles, not strike his pale face with her frenzied hand; and the grieving captive washed her bloodied master, having set out to the waters of the river Simois; she defiled her hair, and she lifted the body of great Achilles and his very great bones in her small hand; when neither Peleus was present for you, nor your sea-blue mother, nor Deidamia of Scyros with her widowed husband.
# literal_translation = Nor not lifeless embracing Briseis Achilles pale with-frenzied strikes face with-hand; and master washed grieving captive bloodied, having-been-set-out to-waters in Simois shallows, and-defiled hair, and of-great body of-Achilles and-greatest in small lifted bones with-hand; when to-you neither Peleus was-present nor sea-blue mother, Scyrian nor widowed Deidamia with-husband.
