# text = deinde, ubi pertuleris, quos dicit fama labores Herculis, ut scribat "Muneris ecquid habes?" cernere uti possis vultum custodis amari, captus et immunda saepe latere casa, quam care semel in toto nox vertitur anno!
# prose_translation = Then, when you have endured the labors of Hercules that rumor tells of, so that she may write "Do you have any reward?" so that you may see the face of the bitter guard, and, captured, often hide in a filthy hut, how dear is the night that turns once in the whole year!
