# sent_id = 2.24a.7
# text = tu mea compones et dices "Ossa, Properti, haec tua sunt: eheu tu mihi certus eras, certus eras eheu, quamvis nec sanguine avito nobilis et quamvis navita dives eras." nil ego non patiar, numquam me iniuria mutat: ferre ego formosam nullum onus esse puto.
# prose_translation = You will arrange my bones and say, "Bones of Propertius, these are yours: alas, you were certain to me, certain you were, alas, although not noble by ancestral blood and although you were a rich sailor." I will suffer nothing, never does injury change me: I think bearing a beautiful woman is no burden.
# literal_translation = You my bones will arrange and will say "Bones, Propertius, these yours are: alas you to me certain were, certain were alas, although neither by blood ancestral noble and although sailor rich were." Nothing I not will suffer, never me injury changes: to bear beautiful no burden to be I think.
