# sent_id = 3.1.10
# text = mollia, Pegasides, date vestro serta poetae : non faciet capiti dura corona meo, at mihi quod vivo detraxerit invida turba, post obitum duplici faenore reddit . . onus; omnia post obitum fingit maiora vetustae: maius ab exsequiis nomen in ora venit.
# prose_translation = Muses, give soft garlands to your poet: a hard crown will not suit my head, but what the envious crowd has taken away from me while I live, after death it returns the burden with double interest; after death old age makes everything greater: a greater name comes to the lips from funeral rites.
