# sent_id = 3.3.6
# text = hic erat affixis viridis spelunca lapillis, pendebantque cavis tympana pumicibus, ergo Musarum et Sileni patris imago fictilis et calami, Pan Tegeaee, tui; et Veneris dominae volucres, mea turba, columbae tingunt Gorgoneo punica rostra lacu ; diversaeque novem sortitae rura Puellae exercent teneras in sua dona manus: haec hederas legit in thyrsos, haec carmina nervis aptat, at illa manu texit utraque rosam.
# prose_translation = Here was a green cave set with mosaic pebbles, and drums hung from the hollow pumice; hence the clay image of the Muses and father Silenus, and of your reed pipe, Pan of Tegea; and the winged doves of mistress Venus, my own flock, dip their crimson beaks in the Gorgon's pool; and the nine Maidens, having drawn their allotted countryside, exercise their tender hands on their own gifts: one gathers ivy for thyrsus-staves, one fits songs to strings, but that one wove a rose with both hands.
# literal_translation = Here was green cave with-affixed pebbles, and-hung hollow drums from-pumice, therefore of-Muses and of-Silenus father image clay and of-reed, Pan Tegean, of-you; and of-Venus mistress winged, my flock, doves dip Gorgonian crimson beaks in-pool; and-diverse nine having-allotted fields Maidens exercise tender in their gifts hands: this ivy gathers for thyrsus, this songs to-strings fits, but that with-hand wove both rose.
