# prose_translation = If my dreams do not sing vain things, Lygdamus, I call you to witness, the punishment will be late but ample before my feet; and a rotten spider will be woven in the empty bed: on those nights Venus herself will sleep. If the girl has complained to you with true feelings, run again, Lygdamus, by this same route, and bring back my commands with many tears, that there is anger, not deceit, in my love, that I too, placed on a similar fire, am tortured: I will swear to be whole for twice six days.
