# text = o centum aequoreae Nereo genitore puellae, et tu materno tracta dolore Thetis ; vos decuit lasso supponere bracchia mento : non poterat vestras ille gravare manus : at tu, saeve Aquilo, numquam mea vela videbis : aute fores dominae condar oportet iners.
# prose_translation = O hundred sea-nymphs, daughters of Nereus, and you, Thetis, touched by your mother's grief; it was fitting for you to place your arms beneath his weary chin: he could not burden your hands; but you, cruel Aquilo, will never see my sails: rather, I ought to be buried, inactive, before my mistress's door.
# literal_translation = O hundred sea-born girls with Nereus as father, and you, Thetis, touched by maternal grief; you (pl.) it befitted to place arms under his weary chin: not could he burden your hands: but you, savage Aquilo, never my sails will you see: rather before the door of my mistress I should be buried, inactive.
