# sent_id = 3.8.5
# text = quae mulier gravida iactat convicia lingua, et Veneris magnae volvitur ante pedes, custodum gregibus circa se stipat euntem, seu sequitur medias, Maenas ut icta, vias, seu timidam crebro dementia somnia terrent, seu miseram in tabula picta puella movet : his ego tormentis animi sum verus haruspex, has didici certo saepe in amore notas.
# prose_translation = What woman, pregnant, hurls insults with her tongue, and rolls before the feet of great Venus, she crowds around herself with herds of guards as she goes, whether she follows the middle streets, like a Maenad struck, or frequent madness-terrors frighten the timid one, or a painted girl moves the wretched one in a picture: of these torments of the mind I am a true seer, these signs I have learned often in certain love.
# literal_translation = What woman pregnant hurls insults with-tongue, and of-Venus great rolls before feet, of-guards with-herds around herself she-crowds going, whether she-follows middle, Maenad as struck, streets, or timid frequent madness dreams frighten, or wretched in picture painted girl moves : with-these I torments of-mind am true seer, these I-have-learned certain often in love signs.
