# text = gloria Lysippo est animosa effingere signa; exactis Calamis se mihi iactat equis; in Veneris tabula summam sibi poscit Apelles ; Parrhasius parva vindicat arte locum ; argumenta magis sunt Mentoris addita formae ; at Myos exiguum flectit acanthus iter; Phidiacus signo se Iuppiter ornat eburno ; Praxitelen propria vindicat urbe lapis.
# prose_translation = It is the glory of Lysippus to fashion statues full of spirit; Calamis boasts to me of his finished horses; Apelles claims the highest place for himself in the painting of Venus; Parrhasius wins his place by a small art; more are the details added to the form of Mentor; but the acanthus bends its slender path at Myos; Phidian Jupiter adorns himself with an ivory statue; and the stone claims Praxiteles in his own city.
