# sent_id = 3.18.1
# text = CLAVSVS ab umbroso qua ludit pontus Averno umida Baiarum stagna tepentis aquae, qua iacet et Troiae tubicen Misenus harena, et sonat Herculeo structa labore via ; hic, ubi, mortales dexter cum quaereret urbes, cymbala Thebano concrepuere deo :— at nunc invisae magno cum crimine Baiae, quis deus in vestra constitit hostis aqua ?— his pressus Stygias vultum demisit in undas, errat et in vestro spiritus ille lacu.
# prose_translation = Closed off where the sea plays by the shady Avernus, the damp pools of Baiae with their warm water, where also lies Misenus, trumpeter of Troy, on the sand, and the road built by Herculean toil resounds; here, when the favorable god was seeking mortal cities, the cymbals clashed for the Theban god:— but now hated Baiae with great crime, what god has stood as an enemy in your water?— pressed by these, he let his face down into the Stygian waves, and that spirit wanders in your lake.
# literal_translation = Closed off from shady where plays sea Avernus damp pools of-Baiae of-warm water, where lies and of-Troy trumpeter Misenus on-sand, and sounds by-Herculean built labor road ; here, where, mortal cities favorable when he-was-seeking, cymbals for-Theban clashed god :— but now hated with-great crime Baiae, what god in your stood enemy water ?— by-these pressed Stygian face he-sent-down into waves, wanders and in your spirit that lake.
