# sent_id = 4.1a.9
# text = quippe Lupercus, equi dum saucia protegit ora, heu sibi prolapso non bene cavit equo ; Gallus at, in castris dum credita signa tuetur, concidit ante aquilae rostra cruenta suae : fatales pueri, duo funera matris avarae!
# prose_translation = Indeed Lupercus, while he protects the wounded face of his horse, alas, did not take good care of himself when the horse slipped; but Gallus, while he guards the entrusted standards in camp, fell before the bloody beak of his own eagle: fatal boys, two deaths for a greedy mother!
# literal_translation = Indeed Lupercus, of-horse while wounded protects face, alas for-himself having-slipped not well took-care horse ; Gallus but, in camp while entrusted standards guards, fell before of-eagle beak bloody his-own : fatal boys, two deaths of-mother greedy!
