# sent_id = 4.4.9
# text = saepe illa immeritae causata est omina lunae, et sibi tingendas dixit in amne comas: saepe tulit blandis argentea lilia Nymphis, Romula ne faciem laederet hasta Tati : dumque subit primo Capitolia nubila fumo, rettulit hirsutis bracchia secta rubis, et sua Tarpeia residens ita flevit ab arce vulnera, vicino non patienda Iovi: "Ignes castrorum et Tatiae praetoria turmae et famosa oculis arma Sabina meis, o utinam ad vestros sedeam captiva Penates, dum captiva mei conspicer esse Tati!
# prose_translation = Often she pleaded the omen of an undeserved moon, and said that her hair must be dyed in the river: often she brought silver lilies to the charming Nymphs, lest Romulus' spear should harm her face: and while she was climbing the Capitol, clouded with early smoke, she reported her arms torn by the rough brambles, and sitting on the Tarpeian rock she wept thus over her wounds, not to be endured by neighboring Jupiter: "O fires of the camp and the headquarters of Tatius' troop and the Sabine arms famous to my eyes, O would that I might sit as a captive at your hearths, while I am seen to be a captive of my Tatius!
# literal_translation = Often she the undeserved pleaded omen of-moon, and to-herself to-be-dyed said in river hair: often she-brought to-charming silver lilies Nymphs, Romulan lest face should-harm spear of-Tatius : and-while she-was-climbing first Capitol clouded with-smoke, she-reported with-rough arms torn brambles, and her Tarpeian sitting thus she-wept from citadel wounds, by-neighboring not to-be-endured Jupiter: "Fires of-camp and of-Tatius headquarters of-troop and famous to-eyes arms Sabine my, O would-that at-your I-may-sit captive hearths, while captive of-my I-may-be-seen to-be Tatius!
