# sent_id = 4.5.5
# text = exercebat opus verbis heu blanda perure / ceu blanda perure saxosamque forat ferat . . culpa viam : "Si te Eoa derorantum / etc. iuvat aurea ripa, et quae sub Tyria concha superbit aqua, Eurypylique placet Coae textura Minervae, sectaque ab Attalicis putria signa toris, seu quae palmiferae mittunt venalia Thebae, murreaque in Parthis pocula cocta focis; sperne fidem, provolve deos, mendacia vincant, frange frangent damnosae iura pudicitiae!
# prose_translation = She was practicing her work with words, alas, burning flatteringly, burning flatteringly, and she bores through the rocky road with fault... If the golden bank of the East delights you, and the shell that boasts beneath Tyrian water, and the fabric of Coan Minerva pleases you, and the rotten statues cut from Attalic couches, or whatever Thebes of the palm trees sends for sale, and myrrhine cups baked in Parthian hearths; spurn faith, overturn the gods, let lies prevail, break the laws of ruinous chastity!
# literal_translation = She was practicing work with words alas flatteringly burning / as flatteringly burning and rocky road she bores through fault... : "If you the Eoan golden bank delights, and which under Tyrian water shell boasts, and Eurypylus's Coan Minerva's texture pleases, and cut from Attalic couches rotten statues, or which palm-bearing Thebes sends for sale, and myrrhine in Parthian hearths cups baked; spurn faith, overturn gods, lies let them prevail, break the laws of ruinous chastity!
