# sent_id = 4.7.20
# text = nam gemina est sedes turpem sortita per amnem, turbaque diversa remigat omnis aqua : una Clytaemestrae stuprum vehit, altera Cressae portat mentitae lignea monstra bovis: ecce coronato pars altera parta phaselo, mulcet ubi Elysias aura beata rosas, qua quaerar ut unda Cybelles mitratisque sonant Lydia plectra choris.
# prose_translation = For there is a twin abode, allotted by lot across the shameful river, and the whole crowd rows with different water: one carries Clytemnestra's crime, the other carries the wooden monster of the lying Cretan woman: behold, another part is obtained with a garlanded boat, where a blessed breeze soothes the Elysian roses, where I may complain, as the wave of Cybele and the Lydian plectra resound with turbaned choruses.
# literal_translation = For twin is the abode having-obtained by-lot across the shameful river, and the crowd with-different water rows all: one carries Clytemnestra's crime, the other of-the-Cretan-woman carries the-wooden monster of-the-lying cow: behold, with-garlanded boat another part is-obtained, soothes where Elysian roses a-blessed breeze, where I-may-complain as the-wave of-Cybele and-with-turbaned choruses sound Lydian plectra.
