# text = Andromedeque et Hypermestre sine fraude maritae narrant historiae . . suae, haec sua summa eternis queritur livere catenis bracchia nec meritas frigida saxa manus; narrat Hypermestre magnum ausas esse sorores, in scelus hoc animum non valuisse suum.
# prose_translation = Andromeda and Hypermestra, wives without deceit, their stories tell; the one complains that her arms are bruised by eternal chains and her deserving hands by cold rocks; Hypermestra tells that her sisters dared a great crime, but that her own heart was not strong enough for this wickedness.
