# sent_id = 4.7.24
# text = pelle hederam tumulo, mihi quae pugnante corymbo molli contortis alligat ossa comis; ramosis Anio qua pomifer incubat arvis, et numquam Herculeo numine pallet ebur; hic carmen media dignum me scribe columna, sed breve, quod currens vector ab urbe legat: HIC TIBVRTINA IACET AVREA CYNTHIA TERRA: ACCESSIT RIPAE LAVS, ANIENE, TVAE.
# prose_translation = Drive the ivy from the tomb, which with its clustering berries binds my soft bones with twisted tendrils; where the fruit-bearing Anio lies upon the branching fields, and the ivory never pales by Hercules' power; here write a song worthy of me on the middle column, but brief, so that a traveler hurrying from the city may read it: Here lies golden Cynthia in Tibur's soil: glory has come to your bank, Anio.
# literal_translation = Drive away ivy from-tomb, which for-me with-fighting cluster binds soft bones with-twisted tendrils; on-branching Anio where fruit-bearing lies-on fields, and never by-Herculean power pales ivory; here song on-middle worthy of-me write column, but brief, which running traveler from city may-read: Here Tiburtine lies golden Cynthia in-earth: has-come to-bank glory, Anio, of-yours.
