# sent_id = 4.9.5
# text = Maenalio iacuit pulsus tria tempora ramo Cacus, et Alcides sic ait : " Ite boves, Herculis ite boves, nostrae labor ultime clavae, bis mihi quaesitae, bis mea praeda, boves, arvaque mugitu sancite Bovaria longo: nobile erit Romae pascua vestra Forum.” dixerat, et sicco torquet sitis ora palato, terraque non nullas feta ministrat aquas.
# prose_translation = Cacus lay struck on his three temples by a Maenalian branch, and Alcides spoke thus: "Go, cattle, go, cattle of Hercules, last labor of my club, sought twice by me, twice my booty, cattle, and hallow the Bovarian fields with your long lowing: your pasture will be the noble Forum of Rome." He had spoken, and thirst twists his mouth with a dry palate, and the fertile earth supplies not a few waters.
# literal_translation = By-Maenalian lay struck on-three temples branch Cacus, and Alcides thus said : " Go cattle, of-Hercules go cattle, of-our labor last of-club, twice by-me sought, twice my booty, cattle, and-fields with-lowing hallow Bovarian long: noble will-be of-Rome pasture your Forum." had-said, and with-dry twists thirst mouth palate, and-earth not-few fertile supplies waters.
