# prose_translation = But if my face and the bristles of a lion frighten anyone, and my hair burned by the Libyan sun, I myself performed servile duties in a Sidonian cloak and spun daily tasks on a Lydian distaff, and a soft band caught my shaggy chest, and I was a girl fit for hard hands." Such words spoke Alcides; but to such words the kindly priestess, her gray hair bound with a rosy fillet: "Spare your eyes, stranger, and depart from this revered grove; come, yield, and leave the safe threshold in flight."
